-- title:
--   Bender–Glauberman Appendix C, Lemma C.3: the conjugate prime line $P_1=W_2^y$
-- statement:
--   Develops Steps 3 and 4 of Bender–Glauberman Appendix C, Lemma C.3 (§3, pp. 148–152) on the conjugate prime line $P_1=W_2^y$ with generator $t=s^y$, where $y\in Q$ comes from Hypothesis (B). The element $t$ has order $p$, and $P_1=\langle t\rangle$ normalizes $U$ (unlike $W_2$ itself), so conjugation by $t$ induces an automorphism of the norm-one group $U$ of $p$-power order.
--
--   Main definitions: `P1` (the conjugate prime-line subgroup), `t` (the $y$-conjugate of $s$), `finite_P1`, `tConjUAut` (conjugation by $t$ as an automorphism of $U$), `tConjNormOneUnitsAut` (transported to the concrete norm-one unit group) and `w2ConjQAut` (conjugation action of $W_2$ on the normal elementary abelian subgroup $Q$).
--
--   The bundle also proves 13 supporting lemmas used by later statements.
-- source:
--   Yawara Ishida, Lean 4 formalization of the Feit–Thompson (odd order) theorem, github.com/yawara/odd-order @ 20a6fccbb63c (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/yawara/odd-order/blob/20a6fccbb63c0b138acda9f7fafd798c42f9441b/OddOrder/BG/AppC_LemmaC3_ConjugateLine.lean

